tyle-module-scss-module__ubvNPq__problemDescription"><p>You are given an ar=
ray representing the heights of trees, and an integer <code>k</code> repres=
enting the total length of wood that needs to be cut.</p><p>For this task, =
a woodcutting machine is set to a certain height, <code>H</code>. The machi=
ne cuts off the top part of all trees taller than <code>H</code>, while tre=
es shorter than <code>H</code> remain untouched. <strong>Determine the high=
est possible setting</strong> of the woodcutter (<code>H</code>) so that it=
 cuts <strong>at least <code>k</code> meters</strong> of wood.</p><p>Assume=
 the woodcutter cannot be set higher than the height of the tallest tree in=
 the array.</p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><figure class=3D"py-1"><div =
style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><img alt=3D"Image represents =
